  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is the current best at 0.650 acc, showing that learned encoders substantially outperform PCA (0.591) under the same profile/aggregation settings, and avgpool outperforms transformer for aggregation. Uncertainty: SCGPT is a completely untested encoder—we have zero data on how its learned representations compare to SCVI. Question tested: Does scgpt under the best-known settings (multiprofile, avgpool) match or exceed scvi_n200? This is a clean single-variable comparison to config_005 (only the RNA encoder changes). Why best next experiment: It reduces the most uncertainty by probing an entirely new encoder dimension under controlled conditions. The result directly determines which learned encoder to carry forward into any future multimodal or profile-setting experiments, making it more informative than re-testing aggregation (already strong evidence for avgpool) or jumping to multimodal (multiple simultaneous changes, and image alone was very weak at 0.208)."
